    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "NE 7, BUF 0",
        "text": "Drake Maye hit Romeo Doubs for a 14-yard touchdown with 7:01 left in the quarter, and Buffalo didn't score in the first."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "BUF 17, NE 14",
        "text": "James Cook's 8-yard run tied it early in the quarter, and Rhamondre Stevenson's 1-yard run put New England back up 14–7 with 5:38 left. A Cole Bishop touchdown for Buffalo was overturned on replay, but Josh Allen's 2-yard run with a minute left (his 88th career touchdown from scrimmage, a Bills record) tied it 14–14, and Tyler Bass' 27-yard field goal with 2 seconds left gave Buffalo a 17–14 halftime lead."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "NE 21, BUF 17",
        "text": "Maye's 2-yard touchdown pass to Doubs, his second of the day, put New England back in front 21–17 with 8:15 left in the quarter."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: NE 29, BUF 26",
        "text": "Bass' 38-yard field goal made it 21–20, and Allen's 34-yard touchdown pass to Keon Coleman (two-point try failed) put Buffalo up 26–21 with 4:27 left. Maye answered with an eight-play, 73-yard drive capped by Efton Chism III's one-handed 23-yard touchdown catch on third-and-5 with 1:50 left, and the two-point conversion made it 29–26. Craig Woodson intercepted Allen's underthrown deep ball for Josh Palmer on Buffalo's last drive, and Maye's 12-yard completion to Hunter Henry let New England run out the clock."
      }
    ],
